Split out of k138 (model-scoped capability registry). The boolean capability
registry — even now that it is model-scoped — cannot express a MUTUAL-EXCLUSION
between two capabilities in one request. Two providers (verified 2026-09-01 in
the k138 matrix) reject a body that combines tools and response_format:

  * Cerebras: "tools and response_format cannot be used in the same request"
    (gpt-oss-120b hard-rejects). inference-docs.cerebras.ai/capabilities/structured-outputs
  * Groq: "Streaming and tool use are not currently supported with Structured
    Outputs." console.groq.com/docs/structured-outputs , /docs/tool-use

This directly contradicts ADR 0005 premise (structured output and forced tool
calling are two faces of one mechanism, freely rewritten into each other): on
these two providers they are mutually exclusive in a single request. A caller
passing both tools and response_format to chat_f builds a body the provider
400s, and no single flag can express "these two are exclusive here" (k138
ticket, option 5).

Scope: this is a NEW shape (a constraint between two flags), deliberately kept
OUT of k138 (which only fixed single-flag honesty). Decide the shape: at
minimum a per-engine croak when tools and response_format are combined on
Cerebras / Groq, rather than shipping a body that 400s. Groq additionally
excludes streaming+tools with structured outputs — a three-way constraint.

Foundation to build on: k138 landed the per-model correction layer
(Role::Capabilities::model_capability_corrections) + the engine-wide `around
engine_capabilities` gate. This ticket needs a constraint expression that sits
above the booleans (chat_f-level), not another boolean.

